    <title>Hydraulic Particle Erosion</title>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="md_docs_2content_2dev_2hydraulic__particle_1autotoc_md34"/> This document details the simulation model, kinematics, sediment transport equations, and implementation of particle-based hydraulic erosion (<computeroutput>hydraulic_particle</computeroutput>) in HighMap.</para>
<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2dev_2hydraulic__particle_1autotoc_md35">
<title>1. Overview</title>
<para>Hydraulic erosion models the carving of terrain by surface water runoff. In HighMap, particle-based hydraulic erosion uses a Lagrangian formulation where virtual water droplets (particles) are spawned across the heightfield, navigate downslope according to local terrain kinematics, transport suspended sediment, and iteratively carve channels and deposit alluvial fans.</para>
<para><image type="html" name="../../images/hydraulic_comparison_particle.png" inline="yes"></image>
</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".mermaid"><codeline><highlight class="normal">flowchart<sp/>TD</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>A[&quot;Particle<sp/>Spawn<sp/>(Stochastic<sp/>Position<sp/>&amp;<sp/>Moisture<sp/>Volume)&quot;]<sp/>--&gt;<sp/>B[&quot;Compute<sp/>Continuous<sp/>Gradient<sp/>&amp;<sp/>Direction&quot;]</highlight></codeline>
